<!-- ======================================================================
     THE SWITCHES ARE NOT WRITTEN HERE, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.

     Which parts of a product can be sold separately is the PRODUCT's answer,
     not the cockpit's. So this file carries no records at all: it calls the
     seeder, which reads whatever the product registered and puts it in the
     table. On a machine where no product has registered anything, the table
     stays empty and the screen says so honestly.

     WHY noupdate IS ABSENT (i.e. 0). The call must run on every upgrade, not
     only on the first install: the product's overlay may be installed after
     this module, or gain a switch later, and a seeding that ran once would
     leave the new one missing until somebody noticed.

     ⚠ THE METHOD IT CALLS CARRIES `@api.model`, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING
     (ledger F45). `odoo/tools/convert.py` reads the FIRST argument of a
     `<function>` as the records to call the method on — `record_ids, *args =
     args` — unless the method carries the model-level marker. With no
     arguments and no marker the upgrade dies on "not enough values to unpack
     (expected at least 1, got 0)", and the traceback names THIS LINE rather
     than the method it could not reach. That cost a whole upgrade cycle once.
     ====================================================================== -->
<odoo>

    <function model="biz.feature" name="ensure_seeded"/>

</odoo>
